      "message": "When the $expand GET succeeds but the BMC ignores $expand and returns stub members (only @odata.id), the function falls through and issues a second full GET of the plain collection, even though data.Members from the first call already holds those stubs.\n\nOne wasted network round-trip per chassis on BMCs that silently ignore $expand. The commit message claims it removed a \"redundant second network request,\" but this path still has one.\n\nRecommended change: Reuse the stubs already in hand instead of re-fetching the collection\n\n```\n      Object.keys(firstMember as object).length \u003e 1\n    ) {\n      return data.Members;\n    }\n\n    // BMC ignored $expand and returned stubs; reuse them, don\u0027t re-fetch.\n    return fetchAllMembers\u003cT\u003e(data.Members as unknown as CollectionMember[]);\n  } catch (error) {\n```",
