      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T13:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When the $expand request fails with no HTTP response (network error, timeout, CORS), status is undefined, so the guard is false and the error is swallowed; the code then falls through to the plain-collection fetch.\n\nA transient connectivity failure is reinterpreted as \"$expand unsupported,\" masking the real error instead of surfacing or retrying it.\n\nRecommended change: Only absorb explicit 400/501; re-throw everything else, including the no-status case\n\n```\nconst status \u003d (error as { response?: { status?: number } })?.response?.status;\nif (status !\u003d\u003d 400 \u0026\u0026 status !\u003d\u003d 501) {\n  throw error;\n}\n```",
